  Quote of the Week:

  Pope Julius II, in reply to Michelangelo, who had asked which of his 
artistic tools the Pope would like to try (1506):
  "Nay, give me a sword, for I am no scholar."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  Winter gave way to fragrant spring.  Orin prepared his armies to defend 
Igarka and the surrounding provinces.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Lord Orin for this year.



  Here is the financial report for Orin's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 0 gold in revenue.  0 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  0 
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Orin was left with 5 gold in the 
treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Tilden
To: Orin

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season I set out to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I prepared my armies to defend Sverdlovsk and the surrounding 
provinces.

  Thy humble servant,   Tilden


STATE OF THE NATION:

  My lord and sovereign, greatest of Kings, I humbly beg thy leave to make
